# Sorting Floor public hall. Format: see "Floor layouts" in AGENTS.md.
# World units, the same axes as engine.rs: screen-right is +x+y, screen-down is +x-y.
floor sorting_hall
# Design px of the baked image: width, height, then where world (0, 0, 0) lands.
image 2080 1420 250 680
bounds 0 0 22 14
entrance 1.2 2.8 1 0
landmark 13.9 10.7

# Far walls: the back of the cutaway, tall, never in front of walkable floor.
# Public doors open in the left wall between y 1.8 and 3.8.
block wall -0.6 -0.6 0 1.8 3.4
block wall -0.6 3.8 0 14.6 3.4
block wall 0 14 16.4 14.6 3.4
block wall 18.2 14 19.4 14.6 3.4
block wall 21.2 14 22.6 14.6 3.4
# Near walls, cut down so the courier stays visible.
block wall 0 -0.6 22.6 0 0.4
block wall 22 0 22.6 14 0.4
# Public counters along the front wall.
block counter 5 0 8.5 0.8 0.6
block counter 11 0 14.5 0.8 0.6
# Cropped parcel counter at the turn; the stop door shows past it.
block counter 20.4 3.4 22 5.6 0.9
# Staff sorting aisles beyond a cordon: implied building, not walkable.
block railing 0 4.6 10.2 4.8 1.0
block railing 10.0 4.8 10.2 14 1.0
block rack 1.2 6.4 1.8 14 3.2
block rack 3.6 6.4 4.2 14 3.2
block rack 6.0 6.4 6.6 14 3.2
block rack 8.4 6.4 9.0 14 3.2
# Sorting tables between the public aisle and the loop.
block table 11.4 4.6 17.4 5.4 0.8
# Landmark: the pneumatic exchange tower behind its railing.
block landmark 12.4 9.2 15.4 12.2 5.0
block railing 10.2 8.4 16.0 8.6 1.0
block railing 15.8 8.6 16.0 14 1.0

# Encounter entrances at the junction. Crossing `stop` starts the chamber.
door side 16.5 13.2 18.1 14
door stop 19.5 13.2 21.1 14

route main 1.2 2.8 19.0 2.8 19.0 7.4 20.3 9.0 20.3 13.6
route loop 19.0 7.4 10.9 7.4 10.9 2.8
route side 19.0 7.4 17.3 9.0 17.3 13.6

view arrival 3.5 2.8
view junction 19.0 8.6
view return 10.9 4.0
